WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:03.640
What comes to mind when you hear the word schizophrenia?

2
00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:09.230
For many people, it is a word surrounded by fear, confusion, and misconceptions.

3
00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:12.290
But understanding begins when we look beyond the label.

4
00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:16.410
Schizophrenia is a mental health condition that can affect how a person

5
00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:18.890
perceives reality, thinks and behaves.

6
00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:23.310
Some people experience hallucinations, such as hearing or seeing things others do

7
00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:27.980
not. Others may experience strongly held beliefs that differ from reality,

8
00:00:28.330 --> 00:00:32.770
difficulty organizing their thoughts, or changes in motivation and emotional

9
00:00:32.770 --> 00:00:35.860
expression. But schizophrenia does not look the same.

10
00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:40.780
for everyone. It does not define a person's entire identity, abilities, or

11
00:00:40.780 --> 00:00:45.600
future. One common misconception is that people living with schizophrenia cannot

12
00:00:45.630 --> 00:00:51.010
lead meaningful lives. In reality, effective support and treatment can help many people manage

13
00:00:51.010 --> 00:00:55.590
symptoms, pursue personal goals, maintain relationships and work toward

14
00:00:55.590 --> 00:01:00.330
recovery. Another misconception is that a diagnosis tells us everything about a

15
00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:05.400
person. It doesn't. Every individual has their own experiences, strengths,

16
00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:10.710
relationships and hopes. Stigma can make it harder for people to seek support and feel accepted.

17
00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:15.470
Listening without judgment, learning from reliable information and treating

18
00:01:15.490 --> 00:01:17.570
people with dignity can help change that.

19
00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:22.960
Schizophrenia is a complex condition, and this short story cannot capture every

20
00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:28.340
person's experience. Diagnosis and treatment require qualified health professionals.

21
00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:33.580
The first step toward understanding is simple: see the person beyond the misconception.
